


MKFS(8)             UNIX Programmer's Manual		  MKFS(8)



NAME
     mkfs - construct a file system

SYNOPSIS
     /etc/mkfs special size  [ m ] [ n ]

DESCRIPTION
     N.B.: file systems are normally created with the _n_e_w_f_s(8)
     command.

     _M_k_f_s constructs a file system by writing on the special file
     _s_p_e_c_i_a_l.  The numeric _s_i_z_e specifies the number of logical
     blocks in the file system (logical blocks are 1K on
     2.10BSD.)	The number of inodes is calculated as a function
     of the filsystem size.  The _l_o_s_t+_f_o_u_n_d directory is created
     but the boot block is left uninitialized (see _n_e_w_f_s(8).)

     The optional flags _m and _n determine the block interleaving
     of the freelist that will be constructed, where _m is the
     distance between successive 1024-byte blocks, and _n is the
     number of blocks before the pattern repeats, typically one
     cylinder.	The optimal values for these parameters vary with
     the speed and geometry of the disk, as well as the speed of
     the processor.  _N_e_w_f_s(8) automates the selection of these
     parameters in most cases.

SEE ALSO
     fs(5), dir(5), fsck(8), mkproto(8) newfs(8)

BUGS
     There should be some way to specify links.
























